meta {
  name: Implementation
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_project?project=PROJ-0029
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  project: PROJ-0029
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("has every tab's data", function () {
    const p = res.body.message;
    ["phases", "modules", "training", "integrations", "my_actions", "tickets_waiting_for_you"].forEach(function (k) {
      expect(p[k]).to.be.an("array");
    });
  });

  test("milestones are not included (use Milestones)", function () {
    expect(res.body.message).to.not.have.property("milestones");
  });

  test("status values are lowercase codes", function () {
    const p = res.body.message;
    expect(p.status).to.be.oneOf(["discovery", "active", "go_live", "amc", "hypercare", "closed", null]);
    p.tickets_waiting_for_you.forEach(function (t) {
      expect(t.status).to.be.oneOf(["waiting_on_client", "resolved"]);
    });
  });

  test("modules are in scope only", function () {
    res.body.message.modules.forEach(function (m) {
      expect(m.in_scope).to.equal(1);
    });
  });

  test("my_actions only holds this project's actions", function () {
    const p = res.body.message;
    p.my_actions.forEach(function (a) {
      expect(a.project).to.equal(p.name);
    });
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  One project with what its Overview and Tasks tabs need. The Milestones tab is loaded separately with the Milestones request.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_project`  
  **Screen:** Implementation (Overview, Milestones, Tasks tabs)

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `project` | string | yes | `PROJ-0029` | Project `name`. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** the same fields as a `get_projects` item, plus the lists below.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "PROJ-0029",
      "title": "ERPNext Implementation - Hamza Trading",
      "display_title": "ERPNext Implementation",
      "kind": "implementation",
      "status": "active",
      "start_date": "2026-08-01",
      "end_date": "2026-12-31",
      "days_left": 55,
      "project_manager": "Sahana",
      "stage": "Data Migration",
      "phase": { "index": 3, "count": 8, "name": "Data Migration" },
      "health": "green",
      "percent": 62,
      "go_live_date": "2026-12-15",
      "go_live_days_left": 39,
      "next_milestone": { "title": "Configuration complete", "end_date": "2026-11-20", "days_left": 14, "status": "in_progress" },
      "phases": [
        { "name": "Discovery", "state": "done" },
        { "name": "Config", "state": "done" },
        { "name": "Data Migration", "state": "current" },
        { "name": "Integration", "state": "upcoming" },
        { "name": "UAT", "state": "upcoming" },
        { "name": "Training", "state": "upcoming" },
        { "name": "Go-Live", "state": "upcoming" },
        { "name": "Hypercare", "state": "upcoming" }
      ],
      "modules": [
        { "module": "Accounting", "in_scope": 1, "status": "in_progress", "percent": 60 }
      ],
      "training": [
        { "name": "TRN-0004", "topic": "Selling basics", "trainer": "Sahana", "schedule": "2026-11-12T10:00:00+03:00" }
      ],
      "integrations": [
        { "name": "INT-0002", "integration_name": "ZATCA e-invoicing", "type": "ZATCA", "vendor": "ZATCA", "status": "in_progress" }
      ],
      "my_actions": [ ... same items as Waiting for you, this project only ... ],
      "tickets_waiting_for_you": [
        { "name": "TCK-0112", "subject": "Wrong VAT on credit note", "status": "resolved" }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Overview tab:**

  - `display_title`: show this, not `title`.
  - `status`: project status code: `discovery`, `active`, `go_live`, `amc`, `hypercare` or `closed`.
  - `end_date`: the project's expected end date, or its deadline when no end date is set.
  - `health`: `green`, `amber` or `red` → On track, Needs attention, At risk. Null when not set.
  - `stage`: current stage label as stored: `Discovery`, `Config`, `Data Migration`, `Integration`, `UAT`, `Training`, `Go-Live` or `Hypercare`. Display text, not a code.
  - `phase`: "Phase 3 of 8 · Data Migration". Null when the stage isn't one of the known phases; hide that line then.
  - `percent`: overall progress, 0 to 100 (may be fractional).
  - `go_live_days_left`: negative means overdue, e.g. -3 → "3 days overdue".
  - `next_milestone`: first milestone (of this project's contract type, see Milestones) not yet completed, or completed and waiting for sign-off. Null when none. `status` uses the milestone codes: `not_started`, `in_progress`, `partially_completed`, `on_hold`, `due` or `completed`.
  - `project_manager`: full name.
  - `tickets_waiting_for_you`: tickets on this project waiting for the client. `status` is `waiting_on_client` (we need an answer) or `resolved` (please confirm the fix). A Client User only sees tickets they raised.
  - `training[].schedule`: date-time with offset. `trainer` is a full name.
  - `integrations[].status`: `not_started`, `in_progress`, `blocked` or `done`. `type` is display text as stored: `Biometric`, `Bank Gateway`, `ZATCA`, `Payment`, `SMS`, `Government` or `Other`.

  **Milestones tab:**

  - Not in this response any more: `milestones` was removed. Call Milestones (`get_milestones`) with the same `project`, then use `display_state` for the label and button.

  **Tasks tab:**

  - `phases[].state`: `done`, `current` or `upcoming`. Phases use `name`, not `title`. `name` is the stage label as stored (see `stage`).
  - `modules[].status`: `not_started`, `in_progress` or `completed`. Null when not set.
  - `modules[].percent`: average task progress for that module. With no tasks it is 100 for `completed`, 0 for `not_started`, else null; show `status` then.
  - `modules[]`: in-scope modules only; out-of-scope modules are never returned, so `in_scope` is always 1.
  - `my_actions[]`: open actions for this project only. For the Done list, call Waiting for you with `status=done&project=...`.

  **AMC projects:** this call also works for an AMC, but use AMC instead. For an AMC, `phases` is empty and there is no `phase`, `stage`, `health`, `percent`, `go_live_date`, `go_live_days_left` or `next_milestone`. Instead it carries the AMC fields (`contract_status`, `elapsed_percent`, `hours_used`, `hours_included`, `tickets`), as described in AMC. `modules` may still be filled; the AMC screen doesn't show it.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`; auth errors raised by Frappe don't.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: not this client's project, or the project doesn't exist.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `project` left out.
}
